## Report
Validated the finding at commit e6825c2dd5495f55d3e36fc9b1a2c6e66b28b62c. Code inspection showed the new UI button at src/frontend/src/main.js:1974 calls openURL('https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/camera-osc-does-not-work-unless-camera-ui-is-open'). The frontend openURL method at src/frontend/src/main.js:1022-1025 directly awaits api.OpenURL(url). The backend App.OpenURL at src/app.go:248-253 calls trustedExternalURL before opening. trustedExternalURL at src/app.go:263-273 only allowlists github.com, hatolife.booth.pm, support.discord.com, and x.com; feedback.vrchat.com is absent and therefore reaches src/app.go:271, returning "許可されていないURLです". I added a targeted Go test that calls (&App{}).OpenURL() with the exact frontend URL and checks for the allowlist rejection, plus a control test for a known allowed GitHub URL. Because tests require the embedded frontend/dist path, I created a minimal placeholder directory for go:embed. Command output: `go test ./ -run 'TestValidation(VRChatFeedbackLinkRejectedByOpenURLPolicy|ExistingAllowedExternalURLAccepted)' -count=1 -v` passed, including `TestValidationVRChatFeedbackLinkRejectedByOpenURLPolicy` and `TestValidationExistingAllowedExternalURLAccepted`. I also built a debug test binary with `go test -c -gcflags=all='-N -l'` and ran LLDB non-interactively. The LLDB trace stopped at src/app.go:271 (`return "", fmt.Errorf("許可されていないURLです")`) with backtrace: trustedExternalURL -> (*App).OpenURL at app.go:249 -> TestValidationVRChatFeedbackLinkRejectedByOpenURLPolicy at validation_feedback_link_test.go:12. This proves the UI-provided VRChat Feedback link is rejected by the existing URL policy. Crash validation was not applicable because this is a non-crashing functional allowlist mismatch; a debug test binary ran successfully. Valgrind was attempted but is not installed in the container; Go ASan was also run and passed, as expected for a non-memory bug.

